WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.340
Your money year in Canada, in four lines and one budget.

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:13.290
The Bank of Canada held its rate at 2.25%. Then on October 29, it raised it to 2.50%.

3
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.430
Posted five-year mortgage rates edged up too.

4
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:24.390
But core inflation cooled, from 2.7% to 1.8%.

5
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.260
And the loonie ended weaker against the US dollar.

6
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.490
Then, on November 5, the federal budget.

7
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:42.640
Proposed from this year: a new exemption for some growth-company shares, and a higher bar before you file the foreign-property form.

8
00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:52.370
For 2027: a new tax-filing date, a refundable caregiver credit, and a consultation on an RRSP for life.

9
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:59.570
And for 2028: a higher threshold before tax instalments are required.

10
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:05.710
Every figure here is from its official source. The proposals are not law unless they're enacted.

11
00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.310
Education only, not advice.
Made with AI assistance. I directed and reviewed the work and checked every figure against its source.
This voice is AI-generated.
